      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! Here\u0027s the answer:\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], **the Hub never holds the Anthropic API key in its own process environment at all.** Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **The key is injected only into the child process environment** of the spawned Ingest agent, immediately before that process starts\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** with the credential\n\nThis design ensures that a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only in the short-lived child process that actually makes calls to the Anthropic API.\n\nThe same scoping model applies to the Query agent as well: it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from or stored in the Hub\u0027s process environment.",
      "input_tokens": 5316,
      "output_tokens": 204
    }
